				/>
				<p>
					<span class="font-bold text-orange-600">Kvile</span> (Norwegian for "rest") is a
					lightweight, fast HTTP debugging tool built with Tauri and Rust. Unlike heavyweight
					alternatives like Postman, Kvile treats <code class="px-1 py-0.5 bg-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-700 rounded text-xs">.http</code>
					files as first-class citizens.
				</p>
				<p>
					Works seamlessly with JetBrains HTTP Client, VS Code REST Client, and Kulala (Neovim)
					formats. Features dual editor modes, JavaScript scripting for assertions, request history
					with search, and sub-second startup times. No telemetry, no cloud sync - just a fast,
					privacy-respecting tool for developers.
				</p>
